  "body": "In the Payment Request spec, I have a situation where I need to check if an id exists and throw a DOMException of some sort. \r\n\r\nI noticed that IDB is using \"ConstraintError\": \r\n\r\n> A mutation operation in a transaction failed because a constraint was not satisfied.\r\n\r\nBut the above description is overly specific for my case. I wonder if we should reword the above to be less databasey?\r\n\r\nSame applies to \"VersionError\":  \r\n\r\n> An attempt was made to open a database using a lower version than the existing version. \r\n\r\nshould probably drop the word database, because it could, in theory apply to a any kind of versioned data store.\r\n\r\nAnyway, I'm happy to use \"ConstraintError\" but I'm wonder if maybe we could have a \"NotUniqueError\" or \"DuplicateId\" error? It feels like a common thing. \r\n ",
